  "visualBrief": "Complete mapped garden-house exterior interpretation: two-level apple storehouse with pale log lower room, weathered vertical-board upper room, broad red standing-seam hip roof, open front gallery and external twelve-tread stair. Three lower wooden gate openings and one upper gallery entrance are physically recessed; timber piers, railings, stringers and supported aprons complete the exterior. The independent named garden-house POI and its own mapped footprint remain distinct from the nearby granary. No copied signs, inscriptions, people, merchandise, furnishings or photograph pixels. Hidden rear inventory and precise historical levels remain reconstructed.",
